Subject: [PATCH] sixaxis: authorize PS3 controllers plugged over USB without asking

Complete the cable pairing of CABLE_PAIRING_SIXAXIS devices right away, as
if the agent had accepted it. DS4 controllers still go through the agent.

This is a deliberate local choice (no configuration option): any USB device
announcing 054c:0268 gets paired and trusted. Not meant for upstream as is.

Tested: plug, unplug, press PS: connected over Bluetooth with no prompt.
---
--- a/plugins/sixaxis.c
+++ b/plugins/sixaxis.c
@@ -380,6 +380,17 @@
 	closure->fd = fd;
 	bacpy(&closure->bdaddr, &device_bdaddr);
 	closure->type = cp->type;
+
+	/* A PS3 controller plugged over USB is accepted without asking the
+	 * agent: the closure is completed right away as if authorized.
+	 */
+	if (cp->type == CABLE_PAIRING_SIXAXIS) {
+		info("sixaxis: authorizing PS3 controller automatically");
+		g_hash_table_insert(pending_auths, closure->sysfs_path, closure);
+		agent_auth_cb(NULL, closure);
+		return true;
+	}
+
 	adapter_bdaddr = btd_adapter_get_address(adapter);
 	closure->auth_id = btd_request_authorization_cable_configured(
 					adapter_bdaddr, &device_bdaddr,
